- the Debian packages installed into the image, nor the `mariadb:11` base image
  (see section 3).

## 2. Observium Community Edition (packaged, not owned)

The `observium` container is built by downloading the official Observium
Community Edition tarball
(`https://www.observium.org/observium-community-latest.tar.gz`, see
`OBSERVIUM_DOWNLOAD_URL` in the [Dockerfile](Dockerfile)) and unpacking it
**unmodified** into `/opt/observium`. No Observium source file is patched or
relicensed by this repository; the entrypoint only writes a configuration file
(`config.php`) at runtime.

The license document shipped inside that tarball is
`/opt/observium/LICENSE.COMMUNITY`. Its first lines state, verbatim:

```
Observium License Version 1.0

Copyright (c) 2007-2013 Adam Armstrong
          (c) 2013-2021 Observium Limited
```

The license is named **"Observium License Version 1.0"**. It is not the MIT
license and not a license this repository may change. Among other things it

- permits copying and distributing the Software **in unmodified form**,
  provided the entire package — including copyright, trademark notices and
  disclaimers as released by the initial developer — is distributed with it;
- permits distributing modifications only in a form separate from the
  Software, must not alter or remove copyright notices, and grants the initial
  developer a non-exclusive royalty-free right to distribute such
  modifications in future versions;
- provides the Software **"AS IS", with no warranty**, and limits the liability
  of the initial developers and copyright holders.

The full text is authoritative and travels with the software: read it with

```bash
docker run --rm --entrypoint cat tuantuantuantuantuan/observium:latest \
  /opt/observium/LICENSE.COMMUNITY
```

or from the upstream tarball
(`curl -fsSL https://www.observium.org/observium-community-latest.tar.gz | tar -xzO observium/LICENSE.COMMUNITY`).

Because the image is built by unpacking that tarball as-is, the image contains
`LICENSE.COMMUNITY`, `README` and `VERSION` unchanged, so the copyright and
license notices travel with the distributed software.

Observium also publishes editions and services under their own commercial
terms; see <https://www.observium.org> for what is offered and under which
terms. This repository does not grant, extend or restrict any right in
Observium itself.

### What this repository does and does not claim

| Claim | Status |
|---|---|
| The packaging files in this repository are MIT licensed | yes (section 1) |
| Observium itself is MIT / Apache / GPL / public domain | **no** — it is under the "Observium License Version 1.0" shown above |
| Observium's source has been modified here | **no** — the tarball is unpacked unmodified |
| This project is the Observium project, or endorsed by it | **no** — it is an unofficial packaging |
| The name "Observium" and its logos are ours to license | **no** — they remain with their owners |

If you redistribute an image built from this repository, keep
`/opt/observium/LICENSE.COMMUNITY` intact and include the license text with
whatever you ship. If you need terms other than the upstream license for
Observium itself, ask the Observium authors.

## 3. Third-party components inside the image

The image and the Compose stack install or run software from other projects,
each under its own license and copyright, none of it relicensed here:

| Component | Where it comes from | License (as published by that project) |
|---|---|---|
| Debian 13 (`trixie`) userland | `debian:13-slim` | a mixture of free-software licenses, per package |
| nginx | Debian repository | BSD-2-Clause |
| PHP 8.5 | [`php:8.5-fpm-trixie`](https://hub.docker.com/_/php) image, built from php-src | PHP License 3.01 |
| APCu and the PHP extensions built in the image stage | php-src / PECL | PHP License 3.01 and each extension's own license |
| MariaDB server and client | `mariadb:11` image, `mariadb-client` package | GPL-2.0 |
| RRDtool, Net-SNMP, fping, Graphviz, ImageMagick, ipmitool, mtr, whois | Debian repositories | each project's own license |
| Trivy, actionlint, ShellCheck | CI only, never shipped in the image | Apache-2.0 / MIT / GPL-3.0 respectively |

Exact versions are recorded in the image at `/etc/observium-components` and
`/etc/php-version`, and package copyright files are available in the usual
Debian locations inside the container
(`/usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright`).

## 4. Documentation and screenshots

The documentation in this repository is covered by the MIT license in section
1. The screenshots in [`docs/images/`](docs/images/) show the Observium web
interface; they are included to document this packaging, and the interface
design and the artwork shown in them remain the property of their respective
owners.

## 5. Questions

- Licensing of **this packaging**: open an issue in this repository.
- Licensing of **Observium**: <https://www.observium.org>.
- A vulnerability in this packaging: see [SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md).
